  "summary": [
    "Anchor on annual Mediterranean deaths tracked by IOM Missing Migrants Project; recent pace (≈606 by Feb 2026) implies momentum toward 1,000 by end-April if the trend persists.",
    "Early 2026 data show a high fatality pace, with weather-driven risk and spring crossings adding upside potential to fatalities.",
    "Policy actions and reporting gaps provide headwinds but are unlikely to fully offset the strong near-term momentum."
  ],
  "confidence": "high",
  "narrative": "Starting from the reference class, the observed pace through February 2026 indicates a plausible path to 1,000 Mediterranean deaths by April if momentum continues. Upward drivers (pace, weather, spring crossings) dominate, while policy responses and data gaps offer some dampening, yielding a calibrated, high-confidence near-term estimate.",
  "justification": {
    "anchor": {
      "probability": 0.8,
      "basis": "reference class: annual Mediterranean deaths tracked by IOM Missing Migrants Project; anchor probability reflects baseline strength from prior years’ tallies and the February 2026 pace."
    },
    "factor_updates": [
      {
        "factor": "Early-2026 mortality pace (Feb 2026: ~606 deaths)",
        "direction": "up",
        "magnitude": "strong",
        "rationale": "The pace through February 2026 signals momentum sufficient to push total to >1,000 if continued through March–April."
      },
      {
        "factor": "Adverse weather and sea conditions in the central Mediterranean",
        "direction": "up",
        "magnitude": "strong",
        "rationale": "Storms and rough seas raise risk and can produce spikes, increasing near-term fatalities."
      },
      {
        "factor": "Seasonal migration patterns toward spring",
        "direction": "up",
        "magnitude": "moderate",
        "rationale": "Spring typically sees more crossings, contributing to higher tolls if other conditions remain unfavorable."
      },
      {
        "factor": "Policy shifts and search-and-rescue capacity",
        "direction": "down",
        "magnitude": "moderate",
        "rationale": "Tighter controls and enhanced SAR could reduce crossings and fatalities, tempering the toll."
      },
      {
        "factor": "Reporting gaps and data lags in Missing Migrants Project",
        "direction": "down",
        "magnitude": "weak",
        "rationale": "Incomplete reporting can undercount fatalities, marginally lowering observed counts."
      }
    ],
    "synthesis_rationale": "The posterior combines a strong upward anchor from recent pace with several upward risk factors (pace, weather, spring crossings) and a few dampening factors (policy actions, data gaps). Given the robust early pace, a high probability near 0.98 is plausible, but calibration accounts for data lags and volatility; multiple correlated factors imply some overcount risk in a pure additive view, hence a tight credible range."
  }
}

